From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:30:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] replay: x-rr-end-record, end a recording and keep running

PANDA's end_record.  The log is finalized as at exit (a shutdown event, so
a replay stops at this point, then the end event and the header).  If
x-rr-begin-record switched icount on, icount_disable_runtime switches it
off: the icount timers go, the TCG ops and every vCPU's cflags go back,
TBs are flushed, and the host-driven virtual clock resumes from the icount
time.  The VM keeps running; chardevs and filters left on their replay
paths pass through in replay mode none.

R4 of the panda-next plan.
---
 qapi/replay.json      | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 replay/replay-begin.c | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 replay/stubs-system.c |  5 +++++
 3 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/qapi/replay.json b/qapi/replay.json
index 1325130ecdd21439063f85bb1cb515f5f8d08b63..29c55e07ac0a0eede8db15616c7dde52bb1219de 100644
--- a/qapi/replay.json
+++ b/qapi/replay.json
@@ -195,3 +195,20 @@
             '*chardevs': ['str'] },
   'returns': 'RrBeginRecordInfo',
   'features': [ 'unstable' ] }
+
+##
+# @x-rr-end-record:
+#
+# End a recording started by `x-rr-begin-record` (or -icount
+# rr=record) and keep the VM running.  The log is finalized; a replay
+# of it stops here.  If `x-rr-begin-record` switched icount on, it is
+# switched off again and the guest clock continues.
+#
+# Features:
+#
+# @unstable: experimental
+#
+# Since: 11.1
+##
+{ 'command': 'x-rr-end-record',
+  'features': [ 'unstable' ] }
diff --git a/replay/replay-begin.c b/replay/replay-begin.c
index 514bfee2dc64fb8099d33867b481619907aa2a16..4e3b320c55b596cccc50cc4c84bcf8b847fa85f8 100644
--- a/replay/replay-begin.c
+++ b/replay/replay-begin.c
@@ -6,7 +6,9 @@
  * its replay path (chardevs journalled, filter-replay on every netdev; virtio
  * ioeventfd must already be off), saves an internal snapshot as the start
  * point, reloads it and opens the log.  x-rr-begin-replay does the same in a
- * process started with -S and replays from the snapshot.
+ * process started with -S and replays from the snapshot.  x-rr-end-record
+ * closes the log and, if begin switched icount on, switches it off again:
+ * the VM keeps running.
  *
  * Loading the start snapshot relies on run_on_cpu() handing the replay mutex
  * to a vCPU while it waits (system/cpus.c), which drops and retakes the BQL.
@@ -348,3 +350,32 @@ RrBeginRecordInfo *qmp_x_rr_begin_replay(const char *snapshot,
     vm_start();
     return info;
 }
+
+/*
+ * End a recording and keep running.  The log is finalized as at exit (an
+ * EVENT_SHUTDOWN, so a replay stops here, then the end event and header).
+ * If x-rr-begin-record switched icount on, it goes off again, and the guest
+ * clock continues from the icount time.
+ */
+void qmp_x_rr_end_record(Error **errp)
+{
+    bool was_running = runstate_is_running();
+
+    if (replay_mode != REPLAY_MODE_RECORD) {
+        error_setg(errp, "not recording");
+        return;
+    }
+    if (was_running) {
+        vm_stop(RUN_STATE_PAUSED);
+    }
+    replay_finish();
+    if (icount_by_begin) {
+        icount_by_begin = false;
+        if (!icount_disable_runtime(errp)) {
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+    if (was_running) {
+        vm_start();
+    }
+}
diff --git a/replay/stubs-system.c b/replay/stubs-system.c
index 5a4df130367b5efaca5d80ca1dc29d666473a8e3..e0a389e47a0c00d09afcdcb6f6e9bac082c3c36a 100644
--- a/replay/stubs-system.c
+++ b/replay/stubs-system.c
@@ -116,3 +116,8 @@ RrBeginRecordInfo *qmp_x_rr_begin_replay(const char *snapshot, const char *file,
     error_setg(errp, "replay support not available");
     return NULL;
 }
+
+void qmp_x_rr_end_record(Error **errp)
+{
+    error_setg(errp, "replay support not available");
+}
